Me too!

I vote with both my hands in favor of this... Please let's get rid of
capital letters forever in Lojban!

Probably we are late for such suggestions (aren't the rules for Lojban
already frozen?), but this was my first thought when I met Lojban and
still it is!

I think acute accent is more common in computer keyboards than the
grave accent, but I could be wrong.

Also, the rule should be as simple as possible. I think a diphthongue
has always a stressed vowel and an (or two in case of triphthongues)
unaccented vowel(s). Then the stressed one would have the accent.

In the case of "sautuesrydyfytyn", the one who created the cmene would
probably know where it should be stressed. I mean: where do you (or
the "owner" of the cmene) stress the cmene when pronouncing it? there
you should place the accent.

mu'o mi'e la =E1lbaros

The Spanish accentuation system is so complex and full or
irregularities that we shouldn't take it as a model.

